## Follow-up: Codex P1 finding on PR #3225, addressed before merge

Codex review comment (chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]):
  "For the raw SSE flow used to reproduce this incident, a winning
  guided-topic candidate is always wrapped by buildVertexWakeBriefBlock,
  whose output still says 'This block OVERRIDES every other greeting
  rule' (live-session-controller.ts:613-634), and orb-live.ts:7722-7780
  concatenates that block into the same system instruction as this
  revised block. LiveKit similarly appends the same phrase at
  orb-livekit.ts:1882-1894."

Verified directly against the code before fixing:
$ grep -n "buildVertexWakeBriefBlock\|OVERRIDES every other" \
  src/orb/live/session/live-session-controller.ts
-- confirmed: buildVertexWakeBriefBlock (line 594) returns a block
   containing "This block OVERRIDES every other greeting rule..." AND
   quoted examples 'Do NOT say "Wie kann ich dir helfen?" / "How can I
   help?" / ...' — BOTH trigger-pattern classes VTID-03785 already fixed
   elsewhere, present in ONE block.
$ -- confirmed shouldInjectWakeBriefOverrideBlock(isReconnectStart, dedupeKey)
   returns `!isReconnectStart || isPendingGuidedTopicResume` — true for
   EVERY fresh session with a wake-brief winner, not just guided-topic
   ones. Explains why an ordinary session in the live retest ALSO likely
   carried this block yet still succeeded (consistent with the known
   ~36% ambient baseline — not 0% — this block class is a plausible
   contributor there too, not exclusively a guided-topic defect).
$ -- confirmed session.wakeBriefOverrideBlock is concatenated into the
   same system-instruction string as session.guidedTopicNarrationContent
   in orb-live.ts (~line 7722-7781, read directly).
$ -- read orb-livekit.ts:1882-1894, confirmed firstTurnSuppressionDirective
   carries the identical two-pattern combo for the LiveKit transport.

Fixed both:
  - live-session-controller.ts: buildVertexWakeBriefBlock — removed the
    override/precedence sentence and the 4 quoted example phrases.
  - orb-livekit.ts: firstTurnSuppressionDirective — removed the override/
    precedence sentence and the 1 quoted example phrase.

$ npx tsc --noEmit
(clean, exit 0)

Added tests to vertex-wake-brief-override.characterization.test.ts:
  - buildVertexWakeBriefBlock: does NOT assert override, does NOT quote
    examples, still instructs the verbatim first-turn line.
  - orb-livekit.ts source: does NOT assert override, does NOT quote the
    "How can I help?" example.

